cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use spectrl, please cite this software using these metadata."
title: "spectrl: URL-safe interchange for mass spectra"
abstract: >-
  spectrl defines and implements a URL-safe interchange format for individual
  mass spectra. A spectrl.v1 token contains peak arrays, precursor information,
  modeled metadata based on mzML controlled-vocabulary terms, and an optional
  ProForma interpretation. The payload is encoded as CBOR and Base64url text
  with a CRC-32 checksum. Peak arrays can use MS-Numpress compression or
  lossless floating-point storage. Because the spectrum is carried in the
  token, it can be placed in URL fragments, query parameters, data URIs, QR
  codes, notebooks, and publication supplements without requiring a repository
  lookup or application backend. The Python package provides encoding,
  decoding, validation, URL helpers, a command-line interface, and conversion
  from mzmlpy spectrum objects. An independent TypeScript implementation
  supports browsers and Node, and shared conformance vectors test agreement
  between the two implementations. spectrl is intended for self-contained
  spectrum exchange and application handoffs. Repository-based identifiers
  remain more appropriate when persistent archival lookup is the primary goal.
